1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,200
Vibe Arena helps a stream community shape
games and play together. Some

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:15,000
people open the game. Others stay in
Twitch chat. The creators remain visible.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,250
The Studio collects ideas and ballots.
This recorded trial

4
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:26,806
used an owner-selected proposal, with zero
audience votes.

5
00:00:26,806 --> 00:00:33,056
After exact input approval and fresh guest
login, the

6
00:00:33,056 --> 00:00:40,000
controller sent Lantern Table to Codex in
a private VM.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,714
Codex returned source in about forty-eight
seconds. Another

8
00:00:45,714 --> 00:00:52,857
VM ran nine protocol checks, then both
guests were destroyed.

9
00:00:52,857 --> 00:00:58,571
Dispatch through testing and cleanup took
about sixty-three

10
00:00:58,571 --> 00:01:04,286
seconds. The owner reviewed the exact
version. This

11
00:01:04,286 --> 00:01:10,000
preview is static; two gameplay issues
remain documented.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,192
Game, art and idea credits stay outside
game-controlled drawing.

13
00:01:15,192 --> 00:01:19,808
Grove uses curated Kenney CC0 artwork,
without endorsement.

14
00:01:19,808 --> 00:01:25,000
Lantern Table uses code-drawn art and no
external assets.

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,357
The streamer can prepare a VM while chat
discusses ideas,

16
00:01:30,357 --> 00:01:35,714
extend its bounded deadline, or close it.
These new controls

17
00:01:35,714 --> 00:01:40,000
have local mock coverage; live renewal
remains unverified.

18
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,385
Grove remains a reviewed playable example.
Browser actions

19
00:01:45,385 --> 00:01:51,442
and Twitch commands grow the same garden.
Three distinct

20
00:01:51,442 --> 00:01:56,827
accounts can trigger a weather bonus.
Moderators can

21
00:01:56,827 --> 00:02:02,212
pause chat effects while browser play
continues. This

22
00:02:02,212 --> 00:02:08,269
shot shows a requested fallback, with
Marble Race last

23
00:02:08,269 --> 00:02:15,000
in the configured order. Two entrants can
start a race.

24
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:21,286
The initial prototype was Devin-assisted.
Codex implemented the later Twitch, studio

25
00:02:21,286 --> 00:02:28,714
and isolation work. The local suite passes
270 checks. Browser and guest checks

26
00:02:28,714 --> 00:02:35,000
are recorded separately; automated checks
do not establish human gameplay quality.

27
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,556
Next are gameplay validation and a
separate approved runtime. Creator

28
00:02:40,556 --> 00:02:45,000
discovery and clips preserving attribution
remain future work.
